      "writtenOn": "2021-08-30T21:14:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the variadic constructors lack position info. I don\u0027t know of a way to solve this - you can fake default parameters with variadic templates by checking the type of the last parameter, but that only allows you to detect the presence of the extra parameter. It doesn\u0027t let you fill it in with Position::Capture() (which of course has to run in the calling context). Is there some way to do this I\u0027m not aware of?\n\nIn any case I don\u0027t think it\u0027s the end of the world, as you\u0027ll still get a stack trace pointing you right to the error.",
      "parentUuid": "ea85c019_59efea9a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 43,
        "startChar": 73,
        "endLine": 43,
        "endChar": 89
      },
